{% extends "base.html.twig" %}
{% block body %}
  <section class="my-5" aria-labelledby="privacy-title">
    <h1 id="privacy-title">Privacy notice</h1>
    <div class="alert alert-warning" role="note">
      <strong>Project status:</strong>
      This is currently a local exercise project, not a professional or
      production service. This notice is not legal advice. Before making the
      application publicly available, the operator must review and complete
      the contact, hosting, and legal-basis information below.
    </div>

    <h2>Data controller</h2>
    <p>
      The project is operated by Abdullah Alaswad. A postal address and a
      contact address for privacy requests have not yet been provided and must
      be added before public deployment.
    </p>

    <h2>Personal data processed</h2>
    <p>Depending on how the application is used, it may process:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>account details, including usernames, email addresses, and password data;</li>
      <li>
        participant names, email addresses, and answers submitted to
        questionnaires;
      </li>
      <li>
        session data needed to maintain sign-in state and manage participation.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      <strong>Password storage:</strong> The application currently stores
      passwords as MD5 hashes rather than in plaintext. MD5 is not suitable
      for password storage by modern security standards; this is a known
      security limitation and the application should not be used for real
      accounts or sensitive information.
    </p>

    <h2>Why data is processed</h2>
    <p>
      Data is used to manage accounts and questionnaires, enable participation,
      and associate submitted answers with the relevant questionnaire.
      Questionnaire creators can view responses submitted to their
      questionnaires.
    </p>

    <h2>Sessions and cookies</h2>
    <p>
      The application uses technically necessary session cookies to maintain
      sign-in state and participation across requests. These cookies are not
      used for cross-site advertising or tracking.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting and recipients</h2>
    <p>
      Any future server hosting is intended to be in Germany. The hosting
      provider and its privacy information have not yet been specified. In
      local use, data is stored in the database configured for that
      installation.
    </p>
    <p>
      The application does not currently integrate with external APIs or
      analytics or tracking services, and it does not load its scripts or
      stylesheets from third-party CDNs. Frontend assets such as Bootstrap,
      jQuery, and Font Awesome are served from this installation. Questionnaire
      responses are available to the creators of the relevant questionnaires
      within the application.
    </p>

    <h2>Data retention</h2>
    <p>
      The application does not currently enforce an automatic deletion
      schedule. Account, participation, and response data may remain in the
      database until deleted manually or the database is reset. A retention
      and deletion policy must be established before public deployment.
    </p>

    <h2>Legal basis and your rights</h2>
    <p>
      The appropriate legal basis depends on how the application is operated
      publicly. The controller must determine and document it before
      production use.
    </p>
    <p>
      Subject to applicable data-protection law, individuals may have the
      right to request access to, correction or deletion of their data, or
      restriction of its processing, and to lodge a complaint with a
      supervisory authority. A valid contact address for the controller must
      be provided before public deployment so requests can be handled.
    </p>
  </section>
{% endblock %}
